n a row withoutany reason (no reason whatsoever for L. and M., insufficientreason in my case - I cast a spell on him which can be percievedas hostile, but this was a 'fooling around' situation and besidesit is not enough reason to pk anyone in any case I would think).After that he insulted us. I thought the rules were clear about how to deal with that.I am not usually very much for revenge, but Mcloud lost about 3 million xp,Leeloo lost her legendhood and I lost about half a million of my hard earnedxp, not counting stats. I am now speaking for all three of us; weagreed we will ask that he be removed and we still think he should be. I have the whole thing logged and will be glad to send it to you if youwish. If your lack of action means you think he should not be removed,please explain your reasons.Thank you,                                             Figura**mangla**To: figuraSubj: pk by doolotzCc: sauron leeloo mcloudDate: Aug 31Each of you have recieved some compensation for the PK.Compensation is in experience.-Mangla**figura**To: manglaSubj: that is hardly enoughCc: figuraDate: Sep  1I dislike inconsistent rules.I dislike favoritism.I know characters you deleted for less.**mangla**To: figuraSubj: enoughCc: sauronDate: Sep  1I make the rules. The previous zero tolerance was in effectbecuase we had a streak of PK's a mile wide and I was tiredof it. So I dealt with it harshly. Now that things have calmeddown, I revoke to policy.Favoritism? Not really, if a player does not cause alot of harmthey are show leniency. By a lot of harm, that means theyhave been here for years and not caused problems except rarely.If they are terinal problems causers, there is no tolerence.Characters I delete are given warning and they STILL failto \"play nice\".-Mangla**guest**To: figuraSubj: yo sracDate: Sep  8itt voltam, de sebaj, mert szaladnom kellett. minden a legnagyobb rendben,udvozlom a vilagot.hussami